    {
      "input": "Thanks *he said to them, after which he decides to give them back the boots*\nYou'll need them more than me",
      "outcome": "success",
      "provider_code": null,
      "attempt": 1,
      "prompt_hash": "89e077a513e43df5",
      "draft": "\"You are too kind,\" Bartolomhew said, though he raised a hand and gently declined the offered boots. \"But no — they were a gift, and a gift returned is a poor sort of courtesy. Keep them. A man who walks as much as you seem to will want good leather under him far more than I. My own are quite serviceable.\"\n\nHe smiled his easy, paternal smile, the boots remaining in Nicco's hands. \"Besides, I would not have you thinking my kindnesses come with strings, or that I take back what I give. Whatever else is said of me in this city, that much is true.\"\n\nHe waited, hands loosely folded, watching Nicco with mild patience. \"So — will there be anything else, my friend, or shall I leave you to your day?\"",
      "issues": [],
